            <ArticleTitle>Treating pain patients at risk: evaluation of a screening tool in opioid-treated pain patients with and without addiction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>182-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients receiving opioid treatment for chronic pain, many of whom were hospitalized with medical complications of substance abuse, were asked to complete a screening questionnaire to help validate a simple self-administered survey. Questions relating to tobacco abuse and prior treatment for drug and alcohol abuse distinguished patients with addiction and pain from opioid-treated chronic pain patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
